WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.359 --> 00:00:07.649
What if you woke up to an unexpected Internet breakdown

00:00:08.230 --> 00:00:12.630
Would you be able to survive without checking facebook for new postings first thing in the morning?

00:00:13.240 --> 00:00:16.229
With no Google Maps to find your way in a strange city

00:00:17.080 --> 00:00:19.619
with a credit card unable to pay for lunch if

00:00:20.289 --> 00:00:25.829
You're watching this video. It means the internet is still going but what if someone or something shut it down

00:00:26.740 --> 00:00:31.410
This is what if and here's what would happen if the internet stopped working

00:00:32.649 --> 00:00:35.879
You could argue this kind of digital detox would be beneficial

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:44.369
We'd take our eyes off our screens and strike up real-life conversations with each other. We've discovered that our smartphones can actually make phone calls

00:00:45.039 --> 00:00:48.149
We bring back fax machines and start making notes by hand

00:00:49.059 --> 00:00:55.349
Well, maybe not fax machines and hey, we'd still have TV to entertain us the world would not fall apart

00:00:55.500 --> 00:01:00.119
In fact with almost 4 billion people having no access to the Internet worldwide

00:01:00.359 --> 00:01:03.869
Half of humanity wouldn't notice a difference in the short term

00:01:04.659 --> 00:01:07.739
But not you mighty internet user you would notice right away

00:01:08.950 --> 00:01:14.880
If the internet suddenly flatlined social media users would start calling each other on the phone

00:01:15.430 --> 00:01:17.879
Overloading the working telecommunication systems

00:01:18.430 --> 00:01:21.479
Unless cell phone towers and telephone lines were also shut down

00:01:22.450 --> 00:01:25.560
Then you'd go back to writing letters and sending them via post

00:01:26.259 --> 00:01:33.989
Forget about Wireless file transfers with no Wi-Fi. You'd have to use a physical cable to connect to computers or a CD

00:01:35.079 --> 00:01:36.939
remember this

00:01:36.939 --> 00:01:44.039
Now think about the economy with financial data generally stored on a server banking services largely depend on the Internet

00:01:44.590 --> 00:01:46.590
Each transfers would be impossible

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:54.269
Your credit card and debit card would become a useless piece of plastic and what about all those bitcoins? You worked so hard to mine

00:01:54.870 --> 00:01:56.870
Well, you know the answer

00:01:56.970 --> 00:02:01.639
On top of that large companies like Google Facebook and Amazon would go out of business

00:02:02.159 --> 00:02:07.489
losing their combined revenue of almost four hundred and forty billion dollars with Google itself having

00:02:07.860 --> 00:02:11.389
80,000 full-time staff hundreds of thousands of people would be left unemployed

00:02:11.970 --> 00:02:15.919
Even companies that only rely on the Internet as a means of advertising would be affected

00:02:16.920 --> 00:02:21.199
Developed countries would lose entire industries and face economic crisis

00:02:21.989 --> 00:02:24.829
What about those countries with just a small internet presence?

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:31.250
They would be affected too as international trade is dependent on the internet. So is the world's transit?

00:02:32.010 --> 00:02:39.170
With no internet access between airports planes ships trains and commercial trucking we'd go back to tracking goods on paper

00:02:39.360 --> 00:02:45.080
This would raise the market value on transported products as it would be more complicated to deliver goods to stores

00:02:45.900 --> 00:02:51.560
At least you could still travel. However, you won't have Instagram to share your travel selfies anymore

00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:57.410
Wonder if the internet shutdown is even possible. Well, not on a worldwide level

00:02:58.140 --> 00:03:02.929
Some countries have actually introduced a kill switch to intentionally shut down the internet and telephone communications

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:08.269
But killing the whole internet is harder than just cutting off a couple submarine cables

00:03:09.120 --> 00:03:14.149
The Internet is a global network of many other computer networks. It doesn't depend on a single machine

00:03:15.239 --> 00:03:22.189
Even if one part of it went offline others would remain functional. So don't worry. You'll still be able to order pizza for dinner tonight

